  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kebbi - Magaji Karaye Groundnut Production and Processing Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Groundnuts Beneficiaries: 299 total (33 women) Description: There is a limited supply of groundnut oil in the market given that production is mostly at the household. Owing to this shortfall in requirement at both the domestic market and coupled with the ban on imported processed oil into the country, MKFCA seek to increase production of its groundnut oil to meet the local needs of Maiyama local government and the neighboring state like Niger, Sokoto and Zamfara state. The grant will enable the group to purchase farm equipment that will reduce cost of production per hectare, .source improved seeds and inputs, coupled with best agronomical training thereby guaranteeing improved .yield of groundnuts and processing in the group cluster.</narrative>
  </description>
